// sub_sequence_branching — Sub-sequence Call + Return (auto-save / return-to-after)
// Call/Return are window-only (C3-F23 FG-Global exclusion; Phase 4b HALTs them in
// FG) — Stay Set opens a window and they run in the background band. Since BG
// commands hold timing_signals (Held, per §3.4b), the return-to-after landing is
// a Stay (which always drives its own tsig at the S_RUN->S_WAIT transition,
// regardless of band) rather than a NOP; the subroutine-body marker (0x00F0) is
// documentation only — verification checks state_number reaching state 6.
// State table:
//   0: Global NOP, timing_signals = 0x0001 (main line, foreground)
//   1: Stay Set (opens the window)
//   2: Sub-sequence Call, offset 4 (D16-D31 = 4) -> jump to state 6, save addr 2
//   3: Stay 1, timing_signals = 0x0002 (return lands here: saved 2, +1 = 3;
//      also closes the window at timeup)
//   4: Global Reset (restart the demo; foreground, window already closed)
//   5: Jump 5 (padding / unreachable halt)
//   6: Global NOP, timing_signals = 0x00F0 (subroutine body, background)
//   7: Global Return (restore -> state 3)
00010700
00000200
00040400
00020011
00000000
00000053
00F00700
00000300
